## 🔌 plugin.xml wiring

<!--
🔴 Cordova has no bundler. A www/ file without a <js-module> entry DOES NOT EXIST
at runtime — no build error, no lint error, no test failure (the tests require()
from disk). Paste the check:

  for f in $(find www -name '*.js'); do
    n=$(grep -c "src=\"$f\"" plugin.xml)
    [ "$n" -eq 2 ] || echo "MISSING or SINGLE-PLATFORM: $f ($n entries)"
  done
-->

- [ ] Every new `www/` file has a `<js-module>` entry in the **android** platform block
- [ ] Every new `www/` file has a `<js-module>` entry in the **ios** platform block
- [ ] Every `cordova.require` name matches a `<js-module name>`
- [ ] The wiring check above produces **no output**
- [ ] Not applicable — no `www/` files added, moved, or renamed

